  "result": "L29 'LAB LEMCO' POWDER (https://assets.fishersci.com/TFS-Assets/MBD/Specification-Sheets/PS-LP0029-V3.pdf)\nciteturn35view0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last month; Content type: application/pdf; Number of pages: 3; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://assets.fishersci.com/TFS-Assets/MBD/Specification-Sheets/PS-LP0029-V3.pdf\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 115\nL0@P0: \nL1@P0: Document Owner Department: QC\nL2@P0: BT-SPEC-0393\nL3@P0: Page 1 of 3\nL4@P0: OXOID QUALITY ASSURANCE PRODUCT SPECIFICATION\nL5@P0: ‘LAB-LEMCO’ POWDER LP0029\nL6@P0: 'LAB-LEMCO' POWDER LP0029\nL7@P0: Description\nL8@P0: A refined product of very light colour. This extract has been specially developed for general\nL9@P0: bacteriological use wherever conventional meat extract is specified. Use with other refined\nL10@P0: ingredients, e.g. Neutralised bacteriological peptone (LP0034) to prepare culture media which do\nL11@P0: not require filtration. Generally used at a concentration of 0.2 - 1.0% (w/v) dependent on\nL12@P0: formulation.\nL13@P0: Physical Characteristics\nL14@P0: Appearance Straw, free-flowing powder\nL15@P0: Absorbance at 450nm (2% soln.) 0.160 - 0.460 units\nL16@P0: pH (25°C) (2% soln.) 7.2 ± 0.2\nL17@P0: Clarity (2% soln.) Clear, bright and free from sediment and insoluble particles.\nL18@P0: Loss on drying Less than or equal to 7.5%\nL19@P0: Chemical Characteristics\nL20@P0: Ash Less than or equal to 15.0%\nL21@P0: Chloride (as NaCl) Less than or equal to 5.0%\nL22@P0: Formol nitrogen 2.3 – 3.6%\nL23@P0: Total nitrogen 11.5 - 15.6%\nL24@P0: Microbiological Characteristics\nL25@P0: The following tests are carried out:\nL26@P0: Test Solution Organism Incubation Result\nL27@P0: Fermentable\nL28@P0: carbohydrates\nL29@P0: 2% + 0.2ml of 1%\nL30@P0: phenol red\nL31@P0: solution and\nL32@P0: Durham tubes\nL33@P0: Escherichia coli\nL34@P0: ATCC®25922\nL35@P0: 35 ± 2°C for 72 hours Negative\nL36@P0: Indole production 0.1% Escherichia coli\nL37@P0: ATCC®25922\nL38@P0: 35 ± 2°C for 24 hours 1 Positive\nL39@P0: Hydrogen sulphide\nL40@P0: production\nL41@P0: 1% Salmonella\nL42@P0: enteritidis\nL43@P0: ATCC®13076\nL44@P0: 35 ± 2°C for 42-48 hours 2 Positive\nL45@P0: Acetylmethylcarbinol 1%\nL46@P0: + 0.5% NaCl\nL47@P0: + 0.5% Dextrose\nL48@P0: Enterobacter\nL49@P0: aerogenes\nL50@P0: ATCC®13048\nL51@P0-1: 37°C for 24 hours 3 Positive\nL52@P1: Document Owner Department: QC\nL53@P1: BT-SPEC-0393\nL54@P1: Page 2 of 3\nL55@P1: OXOID QUALITY ASSURANCE PRODUCT SPECIFICATION\nL56@P1: ‘LAB-LEMCO’ POWDER LP0029\nL57@P1: 1 Indicator - Kovacs reagent\nL58@P1: 2 Indicator - lead acetate paper\nL59@P1: 3 Indicator - Voges-Proskauer test solutions\nL60@P1: Test Solution Organism Control\nL61@P1: Inoculum\nL62@P1: Incubation Result\nL63@P1: Growth\nL64@P1: recovery in\nL65@P1: broth\nL66@P1: 2% Escherichia coli\nL67@P1: ATCC®25922\nL68@P1: 10 - 100 CFU 37°C for 24 hours Turbid growth\nL69@P1: Staphylococcus aureus\nL70@P1: ATCC®9144\nL71@P1: 10 - 100 CFU 37°C for 24 hours Turbid growth\nL72@P1: Enterococcus faecalis\nL73@P1: ATCC®29212\nL74@P1: 10 - 100 CFU 37°C for 24 hours Turbid growth\nL75@P1: Total Viable Aerobic Count\nL76@P1: A 2% peptone solution is further diluted and 1ml amounts are placed in sterile Petri dishes. Sterile\nL77@P1: Tryptone Soya Agar (CM0131) cooled to 44°C is added to the dilutions using the pour plate\nL78@P1: technique. Plates are incubated at 37°C for 18 hours. Colonies present are counted; they shall be\nL79@P1: less than 10,000 cfu/g.\nL80@P1: Thermophilic Spore Count\nL81@P1: A 2% peptone solution is further diluted and heated at 80°C for 10 minutes. 1ml amounts are\nL82@P1: placed in sterile Petri dishes. Sterile Tryptone Soya Agar (CM0131) cooled to 44°C is added to the\nL83@P1: dilutions using the pour plate technique. Plates are incubated at 37°C for 18 hours. Colonies\nL84@P1-2: present are counted; they shall be less than 1,000 spores/g.\nL85@P2: Document Owner Department: QC\nL86@P2: BT-SPEC-0393\nL87@P2: Page 3 of 3\nL88@P2: OXOID QUALITY ASSURANCE PRODUCT SPECIFICATION\nL89@P2: ‘LAB-LEMCO’ POWDER LP0029\nL90@P2: Revision History\nL91@P2: Section / Step Description of Change Reason for Change Reference\nL92@P2: Entire\nL93@P2: document\nL94@P2: Update to new format Update to new format BT-SOP-7767\nL95@P2: Physical and\nL96@P2: chemical\nL97@P2: characteristics\nL98@P2: Change colour from light\nL99@P2: straw to straw powder.\nL100@P2: Change loss on drying, ash\nL101@P2: and chloride to less than or\nL102@P2: equal to. Add formol nitrogen\nL103@P2: limits.\nL104@P2: Change control BT-CC-1811\nL105@P2: Microbiological\nL106@P2: characteristics\nL107@P2: Add limits for Total Viable\nL108@P2: Aerobic and Spore Count.\nL109@P2: Change non-selective\nL110@P2: medium for total viable\nL111@P2: aerobic and spore counts\nL112@P2: from Plate Count Agar\nL113@P2: (CM0325) to Tryptone Soya\nL114@P2: Agar (CM0131)\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nInternal Error ()\nciteturn35view1 [wordlim: 200] Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://www.asahi-gf.co.jp/products/health/medicine/ebios/4946842100019.html\",\"lineno\":null}); \nFailed to fetch https://www.asahi-gf.co.jp/products/health/medicine/ebios/4946842100019.html: (404) Not Found--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n___________________________                                                                ________________________ (https://www.ccap.ac.uk/wp-content/uploads/MR_EG_JM.pdf)\nciteturn35view2 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: application/pdf; Number of pages: 2; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://www.ccap.ac.uk/wp-content/uploads/MR_EG_JM.pdf\",\"lineno\":10}); Total lines: 65\nL0@P0: QF 09\nL1@P0: Media Preparation Recipe Template\nL2@P0: Revision: 002\nL3@P0: Approved: 29 MAY 26\nL4@P0: Created on:\nL5@P0: 29 May 2026\nL6@P0: CCAP (Culture Collection of Algae and Protozoa), SAMS Ltd,\nL7@P0: Scottish Association for Marine Science, Oban, Argyll, PA37 1QA\nL8@P0: Tel: +44 (0)1631 559000 Email: ccap@sams.ac.uk\nL9@P0: Web: www.ccap.ac.uk\nL10@P0: Page 1 of 2\nL11@P0: EG:JM\nL12@P0: NOTE: 1:1 mixture. See separate recipes. Mix then autoclave at 15 psi for 15 minutes.\nL13@P0: EG (Euglena gracilis Medium)\nL14@P0: Freshwater algae and protozoa\nL15@P0: Stock per 100 ml\nL16@P0: (1) CaCl2 1.0 g\nL17@P0: Medium per litre\nL18@P0: Sodium acetate trihydrate 1.0 g\nL19@P0: Lab-Lemco powder 1.0 g\nL20@P0: Tryptone 2.0 g\nL21@P0: Yeast extract 2.0 g\nL22@P0: Stock solution (1) 1.0 ml\nL23@P0: Add the above constituents and make up to 1 litre with deionised water. For agar, add 15 g per\nL24@P0: litre Bacteriological Agar. Autoclave at 15 psi for 15 minutes.\nL25@P0: Reference\nL26@P0: Schlosser UG (1982) Sammlung von algenkulturen. Berichte Der Deutschen Botanischen\nL27@P0: Gesellschaft 95: 181–276. – adapted for CCAP\nL28@P0-1: Reviewed: 29th May 2026QF 09\nL29@P1: Media Preparation Recipe Template\nL30@P1: Revision: 002\nL31@P1: Approved: 29 MAY 26\nL32@P1: Created on:\nL33@P1: 29 May 2026\nL34@P1: CCAP (Culture Collection of Algae and Protozoa), SAMS Ltd,\nL35@P1: Scottish Association for Marine Science, Oban, Argyll, PA37 1QA\nL36@P1: Tel: +44 (0)1631 559000 Email: ccap@sams.ac.uk\nL37@P1: Web: www.ccap.ac.uk\nL38@P1: Page 2 of 2\nL39@P1: JM (Jaworski's Medium)\nL40@P1: Freshwater algae\nL41@P1: Stocks per 200 ml\nL42@P1: (1) Ca(NO3)2.4H2O 4.0 g\nL43@P1: (2) KH2PO4 2.48 g\nL44@P1: (3) MgSO4.7H2O 10.0 g\nL45@P1: (4) NaHCO3 3.18 g\nL46@P1: (5) FeNa-EDTA 0.45 g\nL47@P1: Na2EDTA 0.45 g\nL48@P1: (6) H3BO3 0.496 g\nL49@P1: MnCl2.4H2O 0.278 g\nL50@P1: (NH4)6Mo7O24.4H2O 0.20 g\nL51@P1: (7) Cyanocobalamin 0.008 g\nL52@P1: Thiamine HCl 0.008 g\nL53@P1: Biotin 0.008 g\nL54@P1: (8) NaNO3 16.0 g\nL55@P1: (9) Na2HPO4.12H2O 7.2 g\nL56@P1: Medium per litre\nL57@P1: Stock solutions 1 - 9 1 ml each\nL58@P1: Make up to 1 litre with deionised water. For agar, add 15.0 g per litre of Bacteriological Agar.\nL59@P1: Autoclave at 15 psi for 15 minutes.\nL60@P1: Reference\nL61@P1: Jaworski, G.H.M.; Talling, J.F.; Heaney, S.I. (1981). The influence of carbon dioxide-depletion\nL62@P1: on growth and sinking rate of two planktonic diatoms in culture. British Phycological Journal,\nL63@P1: 16(4), 395–410. – adapted for CCAP\nL64@P1: Reviewed: 29th May 2026\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n___________________________                                                                ________________________ (https://www.ccap.ac.uk/wp-content/uploads/MR_CHM.pdf)\nciteturn35view3 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: application/pdf; Number of pages: 1; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://www.ccap.ac.uk/wp-content/uploads/MR_CHM.pdf\",\"lineno\":10}); Total lines: 20\nL0@P0: QF 09\nL1@P0: Media Preparation Recipe Template\nL2@P0: Revision: 002\nL3@P0: Approved: 29 MAY 26\nL4@P0: Created on:\nL5@P0: 29 May 2026\nL6@P0: CCAP (Culture Collection of Algae and Protozoa), SAMS Ltd,\nL7@P0: Scottish Association for Marine Science, Oban, Argyll, PA37 1QA\nL8@P0: Tel: +44 (0)1631 559000 Email: ccap@sams.ac.uk\nL9@P0: Web: www.ccap.ac.uk\nL10@P0: Page 1 of 1\nL11@P0: CHM (Chilomonas Medium)\nL12@P0: Freshwater Protozoa\nL13@P0: Medium per litre\nL14@P0: Sodium acetate trihydrate 1.0 g\nL15@P0: Lab-Lemco powder 1.0 g\nL16@P0: Add the above constituents to 1 litre of deionised water. Autoclave at 15 psi for 15 minutes.\nL17@P0: Reference\nL18@P0: Catalogue of the UKNCC List of Algae and Protozoa, First Edition, 2001\nL19@P0: Reviewed: 29th May 2026\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n___________________________                                                                ________________________ (https://www.ccap.ac.uk/wp-content/uploads/MR_EG.pdf)\nciteturn35view4 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: application/pdf; Number of pages: 1; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://ww